      "classification_basis": "refused capability retained with typed refusal LEGACY-FLAG-NEVER-IMPLEMENTED: Resolved (agent/v26.8.1-disposition-repair, 2026-07-31): `git log --all -S\"audit\" -- crates/ggen-engine/src/verbs/sync.rs` returns zero commits -- the live sync verb's flag surface (`sync_run(dry_run: bool, watch: bool)`) never had an --audit parameter added and later removed. `git log -p --follow -- justfile` shows `sync: ggen sync --audit true` present verbatim in the commit that first introduced the `sync:`/`sync-dry:` recipes (043a6599c, 2026-06-10) -- --audit was aspirational from the recipe's very first commit, not a regression. This is not a genuine Chesterton's fence: there is no removed capability to preserve, migrate, or roll back to. The justfile's `sync:` recipe is fixed in this branch to run the real `ggen sync run` (no audit-equivalent flag exists on the live verb), confirmed working by a real invocation (`just sync` exit 0, `.ggen-v2/receipt.json` written)."
    },
